engineers determine practical context limits for production workflows."],"color":"green","sourceId":"hacker-news","sourceName":"Hacker News","sourceUrl":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49566388","license":"Hacker News public API (see usage note)","usageNote":"Story metadata is collected from the public Hacker News API; linked content remains owned by its authors.","attribution":"Hacker News / Y Combinator; linked content remains owned by its authors.","collectedAt":"2026-09-04T21:07:06.899Z","approved":false,"qualityScore":100,"recommendation":"build","decision":"keep","discardReason":"","enrichedBy":"gemini"},{"id":"hn-49535363","title":"Sabbatical Goal and Project Planner for Burnout Recovery","summary":"Helps burnt-out tech professionals structure their extended career downtime with meaningful, low-stress exploration projects.","category":"Productivity","difficulty":"Starter","technologies":["Next.js","Go","API"],"source":"Hacker News · Ask HN","datasetTools":"Hacker News public API","whyBuildIt":"People taking career breaks often struggle to balance rest with constructive creative output without falling back into burnout cycles.","suggestedSteps":["Create a guided onboarding flow to help users define personal recharge objectives and time budgets.","Develop a modular milestone tracker that encourages small, pressure-free weekly goals.","Incorporate a reflection journal to capture insights and changing interests over the sabbatical period."],"color":"green","sourceId":"hacker-news","sourceName":"Hacker News","sourceUrl":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49535363","license":"Hacker News public API (see usage note)","usageNote":"Story metadata is collected from the public Hacker News API; linked content remains owned by its authors.","attribution":"Hacker News / Y Combinator; linked content remains owned by its authors.","collectedAt":"2026-09-04T21:07:06.899Z","approved":false,"qualityScore":100,"recommendation":"build","decision":"keep","discardReason":"","enrichedBy":"gemini"},{"id":"hn-49522896","title":"Verified Remote Talent Directory with Structured Filters","summary":"A clean, searchable directory aggregating monthly remote job seeker listings with robust technology and location filters.","category":"Career","difficulty":"Intermediate","technologies":["AI","API","GIS","Next.js"],"source":"Hacker News · Ask HN","datasetTools":"Hacker News public API","whyBuildIt":"Community hiring threads contain valuable candidate data that is difficult to search, filter, and parse manually.","suggestedSteps":["Parse unstructured hiring post submissions into structured JSON records using AI extraction.","Build a map and list interface enabling searches by location, remote preferences, and specific technology stacks.","Add direct contact verification and bookmarking features for recruiters and hiring managers."],"color":"green","sourceId":"hacker-news","sourceName":"Hacker News","sourceUrl":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49522896","license":"Hacker News public API (see usage note)","usageNote":"Story metadata is collected from the public Hacker News API; linked content remains owned by its authors.","attribution":"Hacker News / Y Combinator; linked content remains owned by its authors.","collectedAt":"2026-09-04T21:07:06.899Z","approved":false,"qualityScore":100,"recommendation":"build","decision":"keep","discardReason":"","enrichedBy":"gemini"},{"id":"hn-49565526","title":"Cloudflare Security Configuration Auditor","summary":"Analyzes and scores personal web service security setups across free-tier edge protections like SSL, WAF, and bot mitigation.","category":"Security","difficulty":"Intermediate","technologies":["Web","API","Node.js"],"source":"Hacker News · Ask HN","datasetTools":"Hacker News public API","whyBuildIt":"Developers leverage robust free-tier security features but often lack an automated way to verify their protective posture.","suggestedSteps":["Construct a checklist interface mapping standard security hardening steps for edge proxy configurations.","Integrate automated DNS and SSL header checks against target domain endpoints.","Provide actionable remediation summaries for missing bot protection and rate-limiting rules."],"color":"green","sourceId":"hacker-news","sourceName":"Hacker News","sourceUrl":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49565526","license":"Hacker News public API (see usage note)","usageNote":"Story metadata is collected from the public Hacker News API; linked content remains owned by its authors.","attribution":"Hacker News / Y Combinator; linked content remains owned by its authors.","collectedAt":"2026-09-04T21:07:06.899Z","approved":false,"qualityScore":100,"recommendation":"build","decision":"keep","discardReason":"","enrichedBy":"gemini"},{"id":"hn-49557875","title":"FPGA Streaming Weight Simulator for ML Inference","summary":"Simulates memory offloading and weight streaming architectures for running machine learning inference without static weight RAM.","category":"Hardware & ML","difficulty":"Advanced","technologies":["Web","API","Verilog","Python"],"source":"Hacker News · Ask HN","datasetTools":"Hacker News public API","whyBuildIt":"Rising RAM costs make exploring alternative hardware offloading strategies like streaming weights via FPGAs increasingly vital.","suggestedSteps":["Model a memory controller simulation in Python to test throughput bottlenecks of streaming weights from disk.","Build a visualization dashboard showing activation memory usage versus streaming bandwidth limits.","Document performance trade-offs for running localized small language models under constrained RAM scenarios."],"color":"green","sourceId":"hacker-news","sourceName":"Hacker News","sourceUrl":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49557875","license":"Hacker News public API (see usage note)","usageNote":"Story metadata is collected from the public Hacker News API; linked content remains owned by its authors.","attribution":"Hacker News / Y Combinator; lin