y cleans up locked build caches.","category":"Developer Tools","difficulty":"Starter","technologies":["Docker","Go","Shell Scripting"],"source":"Stack Overflow","datasetTools":"Stack Exchange API","whyBuildIt":"Hanging prune operations can stall CI/CD pipelines and clog local developer storage, requiring a reliable way to inspect and terminate stuck tasks.","suggestedSteps":["Query the Docker daemon API to list active build cache volumes and identify hung daemon processes.","Implement a timeout and force-release mechanism for locked build cache locks safely.","Create a dashboard or CLI report summarizing reclaimed disk space and active cache health."],"color":"blue","sourceId":"stack-overflow","sourceName":"Stack Overflow","sourceUrl":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/80000831/docker-builder-prune-does-not-stop","license":"CC BY-SA for user contributions; Stack Exchange API terms","usageNote":"Question metadata is available under Stack Exchange API terms; user contributions remain CC BY-SA.","attribution":"Stack Overflow contributors","collectedAt":"2026-09-04T21:07:06.899Z","publishedAt":"2026-09-04T15:39:40.000Z","approved":false,"qualityScore":100,"recommendation":"build","decision":"keep","discardReason":"","enrichedBy":"gemini"},{"id":"stack-overflow-80000828","title":"Python List Search Performance Benchmark Suite","summary":"Build an educational benchmarking library that compares different list searching strategies in Python, highlighting time complexities and best practices.","category":"Developer Tools","difficulty":"Intermediate","technologies":["Python","Benchmarking","Algorithms"],"source":"Stack Overflow","datasetTools":"Stack Exchange API","whyBuildIt":"Developers frequently need guidance on when to use simple linear scans versus generators, sets, or bisect for efficient in-memory data retrieval.","suggestedSteps":["Implement various list search patterns including linear search, generator expressions, set lookups, and bisect modules.","Write comprehensive benchmark scripts using timeit to measure execution time across lists of varying sizes.","Generate clear documentation and performance charts illustrating the optimal choice for different dataset scenarios."],"color":"blue","sourceId":"stack-overflow","sourceName":"Stack Overflow","sourceUrl":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/80000828/best-practice-for-simple-searching-item-in-a-list","license":"CC BY-SA for user contributions; Stack Exchange API terms","usageNote":"Question metadata is available under Stack Exchange API terms; user contributions remain CC BY-SA.","attribution":"Stack Overflow contributors","collectedAt":"2026-09-04T21:07:06.899Z","publishedAt":"2026-09-04T15:35:59.000Z","approved":false,"qualityScore":100,"recommendation":"build","decision":"keep","discardReason":"","enrichedBy":"gemini"},{"id":"stack-overflow-80000826","title":"Flexible JSON Number Parser in Go","summary":"Design a custom JSON parsing package for Go that handles large numbers precisely by supporting arbitrary-precision representations without precision loss.","category":"Developer Tools","difficulty":"Intermediate","technologies":["Go","JSON","Parsing"],"source":"Stack Overflow","datasetTools":"Stack Exchange API","whyBuildIt":"Standard Go JSON unmarshaling into float64 can lose precision for large integers, making a customizable number representation parser essential for financial or big-data applications.","suggestedSteps":["Create a custom token decoder using Go's encoding/json package to intercept raw number tokens.","Implement alternative internal representations using structs, strings, or big.Float and big.Int types.","Write robust unit tests verifying precision preservation across extremely large or decimal-heavy JSON payloads."],"color":"blue","sourceId":"stack-overflow","sourceName":"Stack Overflow","sourceUrl":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/80000826/how-should-a-json-parser-represent-json-numbers-in-go","license":"CC BY-SA for user contributions; Stack Ex